id: 18
hanzi: 不耐烦
pinyin: bù nài fán
level: HSK 5
part_of_speech: Adjective

meanings_summary:
  en: impatient; irritated; restless
  es: impaciente; fastidiado; mosqueado; sin paciencia

senses[1]{sense_number,part_of_speech,register,definition_en,definition_es,example_phrase}:
  1 | Adjective | Standard | impatient, annoyed, or irritated by delay, monotony, or tediousness | que muestra impaciencia, fastidio o molestia ante retrasos o repeticiones | 脸上露出不耐烦的神情 (wear an impatient expression)

example_sentences[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 在拥挤闷热的火车站候车大厅里等待了四个小时后，排队的乘客们逐渐变得焦躁不安且很不耐烦。 | Zài yōngjǐ mēnrè de huǒchēzhàn hòuchē dàtīng lǐ děngdài le sì gè xiǎoshí hòu, páiduì de chéngkè men zhújiàn biànde jiāozào bù'ān qiě hěn bùnàifán. | After waiting four hours in the crowded, sweltering railway station waiting hall, the queuing passengers gradually grew restless and very impatient. | Tras esperar cuatro horas en la abarrotada sala de la estación bajo un calor sofocante, los viajeros en fila empezaron a impacientarse y fastidiarse.
  #2 | 无论客户提出多么琐碎苛刻的要求，优秀的客服经理始终保持微笑与倾听，绝不在言语间流露出丝毫不耐烦。 | Wúlùn kèhù tíchū duōme suǒsuì kèkè de yāoqiú, yōuxiù de kèfú jīnglǐ shǐzhōng bǎochí wēixiào yǔ qīngtīng, jué bú zài yányǔ jiān liúlù chū sīháo bùnàifán. | No matter how trivial or demanding the client's requests were, the stellar customer service manager always maintained a smile and never betrayed the slightest impatience. | Sin importar cuán minuciosas fueran las exigencias del cliente, el gestor de atención conservó la sonrisa y la escucha sin mostrar el menor asomo de fastidio.

collocations[6]{hanzi,en}:
  显得不耐烦 | appear impatient
  不耐烦的神情 | impatient expression
  极为不耐烦 | extremely impatient
