  挥手表示不耐烦 | wave hands impatiently
  不耐烦地打断 | interrupt impatiently

idioms[4]{hanzi,pinyin,meaning_en}:
  心急如焚 | xīn jí rú fén | heart burning with anxiety; extremely anxious and impatient
  急不可待 | jí bù kě dài | too impatient to wait; unable to hold back
  焦躁不安 | jiāo zào bù'ān | fretful and fidgety; agitated with impatience
  百折不挠 | bǎi zhé bù náo | indomitable; unyielding patience in face of hundreds of setbacks

character_decomposition[3]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,meaning_es,radical,radical_meaning_en,meaning_component,sound_component,stroke_count,composition_type,etymology_and_mnemonic,visual_mnemonic_story_en,visual_mnemonic_story_es,tone_mnemonic_anchor,cangjie,traditional}:
  不 | bù | not; no; negative prefix | no; prefijo negativo | 一 | one | 一 (sky ceiling/barrier) | 不 (inherent negation sound) | 4 | 单一结构 | Anciently depicted a bird flying up to the heavens but unable to ascend further (negation). | A bird attempts to fly upward but hits an immovable ceiling line (一), indicating 'not'. | Un ave intenta volar alto pero topa contra una línea barrera (一), señalando la negación 'no'. | 51 | MF | ""
  耐 | nài | endure; bear; withstand; patient | soportar; aguantar; tolerar; resistir | 而 | and / facial whiskers | 而 (whiskers/beard) | 寸 (inch/law penalty of shaving whiskers) | 9 | 左右结构 | Originally an ancient judicial punishment (寸) of shaving facial whiskers (而); one who endured the disgrace displayed patience. | Shaving whiskers (而) with an inch blade (寸) tests a man's endurance and patience. | Afeitar la barba (而) con una pequeña cuchilla (寸) pone a prueba la paciencia y aguante del hombre. | 51 | MBDI | ""
  烦 | fán | troubled; vexed; irritated; bother | molesto; fastidiado; agobiado; preocupado | 火 | fire | 火 (fire burning inside) | 页 (head/feverish temples) | 10 | 左右结构 | Phono-semantic character pairing fire (火) with head (页), denoting a feverish headache from agitation. | Flames of fire (火) flare in the mind and head (页), causing intense vexation. | Llamas de fuego (火) arden en la cabeza (页), provocando fastidio e irritación profunda. | 35 | FMBO | 煩

mnemonics_and_roots:
  composite_memory_hook_en: Incapable of (不) enduring (耐) the burning mental heat of vexation (烦) produces blatant impatience.
  composite_memory_hook_es: Ser incapaz de (不) aguantar (耐) el fuego molesto en la cabeza (烦) se traduce en impaciencia manifiesta.
  cultural_and_cognitive_roots: Traditional Chinese medicine links 'fán' to internal heat in the heart and liver scorching the mind; 'bùnài' means inability to absorb this friction, leading to visible annoyance.
  tone_sandhi_and_pitch_modulation: Tone sandhi applies to 不: preceding the 4th tone nài (51), 不 changes from 4th tone (51) to 2nd tone (35): pronounced bú nài fán (35-51-35).

