    燥 | zào | restless; irritable fire radical
    恼 | nǎo | angry; annoyed heart radical
    急 | jí | urgent; anxious

semantic_boundary_contrasts:
  core_nuance: 不耐烦 expresses visible irritation, restlessness, and annoyance caused by waiting or dealing with tedious matters.
  contrasts[3]{id,compared_word,pinyin,analysis}:
    1 | 不耐烦 vs. 着急 | zháojí | 着急 reflects intense worry or eagerness due to running out of time, whereas 不耐烦 expresses annoyance, grumpy irritation, or disgust with delay.
    2 | 不耐烦 vs. 讨厌 | tǎoyàn | 讨厌 means to dislike, loathe, or find someone repulsive, whereas 不耐烦 is a temporary emotional state of exasperation and short temper.
    3 | 不耐烦 vs. 厌烦 | yànfán | 厌烦 denotes being deeply sick and tired of long-term repetition or monotony, whereas 不耐烦 is an immediate behavioral reaction to frustration.

extended_reading_passages[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 快节奏的现代生活催生了太多的浮躁，人们在红灯前频繁按喇叭，在网页加载时露出不耐烦的神色。然而，生命中最珍贵的东西往往需要时间慢慢发酵。学会放下不耐烦，耐住性子等待，才能看清生命本来的从容美感。 | Kuài jièzòu de xiàndài shēnghuó cuīshēng le tài duō de fúzào, rénmen zài hóngdēng qián pínfán àn lǎba, zài wǎngyè jiāzài shí lùchū bùnàifán de shénsè. Rán'ér, shēngmìng zhōng zuì zhēnguì de dōngxi wǎngwǎng xūyào shíjiān mànman fājiào. Xuéhuì fàngxià bùnàifán, nàizhù xìngzi děngdài, cáinǐng kànqīng shēngmìng běnlái de cóngróng měigǎn. | Fast-paced living breeds impetuousness: people honk at red lights and wear impatient looks when webpages load. Yet life's treasures require patient fermentation. Releasing impatience and waiting steadily reveals life's tranquil beauty. | El ritmo frenético engendra impaciencia: la gente toca el claxon en los semáforos y muestra fastidio si una página tarda en cargar. Sin embargo, lo más valioso requiere madurar con calma. Desprenderse de la impaciencia rescata la serenidad de la vida.
  #2 | 在复杂精密的科研实验与工程调试过程中，任何急躁与不耐烦都可能导致前功尽弃。面对海量数据的异常波动与反复失败，顶尖科学家之所以能取得突破，往往正是凭借着把枯燥实验重复千百次而不显丝毫浮躁的超常耐心。 | Zài fùzá jīngmì de kēyán shíyàn yǔ gōngchéng tiáoshì guòchéng zhōng, rènhé jízào yǔ bùnàifán dōu kěnéng dǎozhì qiángōngjìnqì. Miànduì hǎiliàng shùjù de yìcháng bōdòng yǔ fǎnfù shībài, dǐngjiān kēxuéjiā zhī suǒyǐ néng qǔdé tūpò, wǎngwǎng zhèng shì píngjiè zhe bǎ kūzào shíyàn chóngfù qiānbǎi cì ér bù xiǎn sīháo fúzào de chāocháng nàixīn. | In precision scientific experiments and engineering debugging, any haste and impatience can ruin all prior gains. Facing anomalous data and repeated setbacks, top scientists achieve breakthroughs through extraordinary patience, repeating tests thousands of times without haste. | En la investigación científica y calibración técnica, cualquier impaciencia arruina el trabajo previo. Ante fallos y fluctuaciones de datos, los grandes científicos logran descubrimientos gracias a una paciencia tenaz que repite experimentos mil veces sin decaer.
